          "sec_id": 99869798707239880271856964299535405298,
          "title": "DeepONet (Deep Operator Network)",
          "raw_text": "DeepONet was the first architecture to theoretically prove that neural networks can approximate any continuous nonlinear operator. It consists of two components:\n• Branch Network : Encodes the input function (e.g., initial or boundary conditions).\n• Trunk Network : Encodes the spatial coordinates where the output is evaluated.\nBy combining these representations, DeepONet can approximate solutions to differential equa- tions across different domains.",
          "page_start": 2,
          "paragraphs": [
